      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653",
      "widgets_values": [
        "### The number in the corner\n\nIt is not drawn. The plate is the act with its ink lifted off by LaMa; the scan\nabove is the same sheet with the ink still on it. Both go through the one\nupscaler, so they land on the same pixels, and the second Pencil Crop cuts the\nsame corner out of each. Pencil Lift subtracts one from the other and what is\nleft is the archivist's own mark -- pigment, its breaks, and the ink line that\ncrosses it, all photographed.\n\nThe number is therefore whatever the act carries. On the sheet it means nothing\nat all, which is the line the reel says about it.\n\n`pencil` and `pencil_height` on Page File still place the box it is laid into.\n"
      ]
    },
